course: dictionary
lesson: 5458
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word language can mean several things, so the sentence around it tells you which meaning to use. «British Sign Language (BSL) is a full language with its own grammar, different from English.» Here language means a whole system of words and rules that people use to communicate.
explain: Now read «Languages keep changing, borrowing and playing, so the best language skill is curiosity.» Here language means the way people talk and use words in general. The clue is the word skill: you can have a skill for talking and using words, but not a skill for one set of words.
explain: Sometimes language is part of a phrase, and the phrase has its own meaning. «Mind your language» means be careful not to use rude words. When a phrase does not match the single words, read the whole phrase as one unit, then check with a dictionary if you are unsure.
fact: A language is the words that people use to speak and write, like English, French or Spanish.
fact: Language can also mean the way people talk and use words in general.
fact: «Sign language» uses hand signs instead of spoken words, and «British Sign Language (BSL)» is a full language with its own grammar.
fact: A computer language is a set of words and rules for telling a computer what to do.
fact: «Bad language» means rude words, and «mind your language» means be careful with the words you use.
exercise: «Simba means lion in Swahili, a language of East Africa.» In this sentence, what is a language? | A hand sign | A rude word | A kind of animal | *A set of words people use to speak and write
exercise: Ella says sign language is just pointing. What is sign language? | *A way of talking with hand signs instead of spoken words | Rude words used in a playground | Words that are spoken very quietly | A set of rules for a computer
exercise: «Sharing silly jokes builds friendship and helps younger children learn language.» Find and copy one word that means the words people use to talk. | younger | jokes | friendship | *language
test: A computer language is a set of words and rules for doing what? | Writing letters to friends | Cooking dinner | *Telling a computer what to do | Drawing pictures
test: «Bad language» means what? | *Rude words | Long and difficult words | Words written in a history book | Words from other countries
exam: In «English language lessons», what does language mean? | *The words people use to speak and write | A game of hide and seek | A lesson about lions | A kind of computer
